# Arguments of diskd (diskd.service), and its object store. Pods hibernate
# into the object store and come back from it on any node: without one,
# their disks stay on this node and HibernatePod fails. This file holds the
# store's credentials and is root's alone.
#
#   DISKD_ARGS              e.g. "--budget-bytes 17179869184": the local
#                           chunk cache, 8 GiB by default; see diskd --help.
#   S3_BUCKET               the bucket
#   AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID       its credentials
#   AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
#   AWS_ENDPOINT_URL        an S3-compatible store's endpoint, path-style;
#                           AWS's when unset
#   AWS_REGION              us-east-1 by default
#   DISKD_S3_PREFIX         a key prefix in the bucket, for a bucket shared
#                           with others; all nodes that restore each other's
#                           pods need the same
DISKD_ARGS=""
